+# Implementation Plan: Pitter-o-mat Multiplayer Console
+
+**Branch**: `001-pitter-o-mat` | **Date**: 2025-10-13 | **Spec**: [spec.md](../spec.md)  
+**Input**: Feature specification from `/specs/001-pitter-o-mat/spec.md`
+
+## Summary
+
+Design and implement the embedded control stack for the Pitter-o-mat arcade console: Arduino Mega 2560 firmware for LED ring and encoder input, ESP32-S3 touchscreen firmware for menus and scores, and coordinated update/highscore workflows across 2-6 player modes with configurable Joker behavior.
+
+## Technical Context
+
+**Language/Version**: C++17 subset (Arduino AVR core), C++17 (ESP-IDF 5.x), EEZ Studio UI scripts  
+**Primary Dependencies**: Arduino AVR core, FastLED (WS2812 control), ESP-IDF peripherals (SPI, RS485/UART), EEZ Studio runtime, FATFS microSD support  
+**Storage**: microSD (FAT32) on master ESP32-S3 for highscores/config, EEPROM on Arduino for minimal calibration  
+**Testing**: PlatformIO unit tests (Unity) for firmware modules, hardware-in-the-loop regression harness, scripted LED ring simulator  
+**Target Platform**: Custom hardware combining Arduino Mega 2560 + Waveshare ESP32S3-Touch-LCD-4 (480x480) nodes over RS485 and Wi-Fi  
+**Project Type**: Embedded firmware + multi-device coordination  
+**Performance Goals**: 100 Hz control loop on Arduino; <150 ms input-to-visual latency; firmware update propagation <5 minutes  
+**Constraints**: 60 A @5 V power budget for LEDs, deterministic Joker/segment mapping, offline-capable (no mandatory internet)  
+**Scale/Scope**: 2-6 concurrent local players, up to 8 ESP32 displays, 864 addressable LEDs
+
+## Constitution Check
+
+*GATE: Must pass before Phase 0 research. Re-check after Phase 1 design.*
+
+- Constitution file currently contains only placeholders (no ratified principles).  
+- Gate status: **Pass with caveat** — Treat absence of documented principles as no enforced constraints; flag for governance follow-up after Phase 1.
+
+## Project Structure
+
+### Documentation (this feature)
+
+```
+specs/001-pitter-o-mat/
+├── plan.md
+├── research.md
+├── data-model.md
+├── quickstart.md
+├── contracts/
+└── tasks.md                # created during /speckit.tasks
+```
+
+### Source Code (repository root)
+
+```
+firmware/
+├── arduino/
+│   ├── src/
+│   ├── include/
+│   └── tests/
+├── esp32/
+│   ├── main/
+│   ├── components/
+│   ├── ui/                 # EEZ Studio generated assets
+│   └── tests/
+└── shared/
+    ├── proto/              # RS485 message schemas
+    └── scripts/            # flashing & diagnostics
+
+docs/
+├── hardware/
+└── operations/
+```
+
+**Structure Decision**: Split firmware by MCU (Arduino vs. ESP32) with shared protocol definitions to isolate build systems while keeping UI assets versioned alongside ESP32 firmware; documentation captures hardware wiring and operational SOPs.
+
+## Complexity Tracking
+
+No constitution violations to justify at this stage.
