+# Tasks: Pitter-o-mat Multiplayer Console
+
+**Input**: Design documents from `/specs/001-pitter-o-mat/`
+**Prerequisites**: plan.md (required), spec.md (required), research.md, data-model.md, contracts/
+
+**Tests**: Not explicitly requested. Validation will be via manual hardware-in-the-loop checks described in each user story.
+
+**Organization**: Tasks are grouped by user story to enable independent implementation and testing.
+
+## Format: `[ID] [P?] [Story] Description`
+- **[P]**: Can run in parallel (different files, no dependencies)
+- **[Story]**: Which user story this task belongs to (e.g., US1, US2)
+- Include exact file paths in descriptions
+
+---
+
+## Phase 1: Setup (Shared Infrastructure)
+
+**Purpose**: Establish firmware workspaces, tooling, and shared configuration.
+
+- [ ] T001 [P] Create baseline project layout under `firmware/arduino`, `firmware/esp32`, and `firmware/shared` following plan.md structure.
+- [ ] T002 [P] Initialize PlatformIO project for Arduino Mega 2560 in `firmware/arduino/platformio.ini` with FastLED dependency.
+- [ ] T003 [P] Scaffold ESP-IDF workspace in `firmware/esp32` (idf.py set-target esp32s3) and commit initial `CMakeLists.txt`, `main/app_main.c`.
+- [ ] T004 Install EEZ Studio export pipeline by adding `firmware/esp32/ui/README.md` documenting asset sync from EEZ Studio project.
+- [ ] T005 Set up Python tooling environment at `firmware/shared/scripts/requirements.txt` including CRC utilities and RS485 test harness dependencies.
+
+---
+
+## Phase 2: Foundational (Blocking Prerequisites)
+
+**Purpose**: Core infrastructure that MUST exist before any user story begins.
+
+- [ ] T006 Define LED segment map JSON (`firmware/shared/proto/segment_map.json`) covering SpielLED/GrenzLED group assignments for 2-6 players and Joker override.
+- [ ] T007 Implement shared RS485 framing library in `firmware/shared/proto/rs485_frame.py` with header, length, CRC-8 helpers referenced in research.md.
+- [ ] T008 Add Arduino RS485 transport layer `firmware/arduino/src/transport_rs485.cpp` with polling loop scaffolding calling shared framing (depends on T007).
+- [ ] T009 Add ESP32 RS485/UART service `firmware/esp32/main/transport_rs485.c` establishing half-duplex configuration and receive queue (depends on T007).
+- [ ] T010 Provision configuration persistence stubs: microSD loader `firmware/esp32/main/storage_config.c` and AVR EEPROM accessor `firmware/arduino/src/storage_eeprom.cpp`.
+- [ ] T011 Expose `/status` endpoint skeleton in `firmware/esp32/main/http_status_handler.c` returning static payload aligned with contracts/device-control.openapi.yaml.
+- [ ] T012 Document hardware bring-up checklist in `docs/hardware/pitter-o-mat-setup.md` (power budget, wiring, safety) referenced by quickstart.md.
+
+**Checkpoint**: RS485 transport, storage stubs, and core mappings are ready; proceed to user stories.
+
+---
+
+## Phase 3: User Story 1 - Spieler 1 richtet ein Spiel ein (Priority: P1) — MVP
+
+**Goal**: Allow Player 1 to configure player count, select a compatible game, adjust Joker options, and launch the session while other inputs remain locked.
+
+**Independent Test**: Power cycle system, use Player 1 encoder to select 4 players and start "LichtLoser"; confirm ESP32 UI reflects selections, RS485 commands configure Arduino, and non-primary encoders remain disabled until game start.
+
+### Implementation for User Story 1
+
+- [ ] T013 [US1] Implement session state machine on Arduino in `firmware/arduino/src/session_controller.cpp` handling menu navigation, encoder debouncing, and Joker toggles (depends on T008, T010).
+- [ ] T014 [US1] Add ESP32 UI workflow in `firmware/esp32/ui/menu_flow.eezi` and generated bindings `firmware/esp32/main/ui_menu.c` for player count and game selection screen.
+- [ ] T015 [US1] Wire RS485 commands for session configuration in `firmware/arduino/src/session_commands.cpp` and `firmware/esp32/main/session_bus.c`, including acknowledgement handling.
+- [ ] T016 [US1] Implement `/game/session` POST handler in `firmware/esp32/main/http_session.c` mapping request payloads to RS485 commands (depends on T011, T015).
+- [ ] T017 [US1] Ensure non-primary encoder inputs ignored until session active by updating `firmware/arduino/src/encoder_manager.cpp`.
+- [ ] T018 [P] [US1] Persist Joker configuration to microSD (`firmware/esp32/main/storage_config.c`) and synchronize to Arduino on next boot.
+- [ ] T019 [US1] Update quickstart with MVP validation steps in `specs/001-pitter-o-mat/quickstart.md` (add menu navigation checklist).
+
+**Checkpoint**: P1 story complete and independently demonstrable.
+
+---
+
+## Phase 4: User Story 2 - Spieler erkennen Sitzplaetze und Grenzen (Priority: P2)
+
+**Goal**: Visualize seat assignments and LED boundaries for the selected player count, including Joker-specific adjustments.
+
+**Independent Test**: For 2, 3, 4, 5, and 6 player configurations, verify displays show correct seat IDs and LED boundaries illuminate as defined; Joker toggle should update visuals immediately.
+
+### Implementation for User Story 2
+
+- [ ] T020 [US2] Generate per-player LED group tables from `segment_map.json` into `firmware/arduino/src/segment_mapper.cpp` applying Joker overrides (depends on T006).
+- [ ] T021 [US2] Implement boundary rendering routine `firmware/arduino/src/led_boundary_renderer.cpp` using FastLED to light GrenzLED groups continuously.
+- [ ] T022 [US2] Update ESP32 display assignment logic in `firmware/esp32/main/ui_player_rings.c` to highlight active seats based on session config.
+- [ ] T023 [US2] Extend `/status` response to include player seat mappings in `firmware/esp32/main/http_status_handler.c`.
+- [ ] T024 [P] [US2] Add diagnostic script `firmware/shared/scripts/print_segments.py` to simulate ring output for each mode.
+- [ ] T025 [US2] Document acceptance checklist for seat visualization in `docs/operations/seating-validation.md`.
+
+**Checkpoint**: Seat visualization story complete; P1 + P2 functionality independently verifiable.
+
+---
+
+## Phase 5: User Story 3 - Spielablauf mit Echtzeit-Feedback (Priority: P2)
+
+**Goal**: Provide responsive LED and display updates for scoring events and game state transitions within 100 ms.
+
+**Independent Test**: Simulate scoring bursts via encoder or companion API; confirm LED animations and display updates occur within target latency and update session log.
+
+### Implementation for User Story 3
+
+- [ ] T026 [US3] Implement score tracking and event publication in `firmware/arduino/src/gameplay_controller.cpp`, including SessionEventLog emission over RS485 (depends on T015).
+- [ ] T027 [US3] Create ESP32 event consumer `firmware/esp32/main/gameplay_events.c` that updates displays and triggers win/lose animations defined per GameMode.
+- [ ] T028 [US3] Integrate HighscoreEntry updates for supported modes in `firmware/esp32/main/highscore_store.c` using microSD JSON files.
+- [ ] T029 [US3] Extend `/game/session/current` PATCH handler to allow brightness and Joker runtime adjustments in `firmware/esp32/main/http_session.c`.
+- [ ] T030 [P] [US3] Add LED animation presets in `firmware/arduino/src/animations/` (win_wave.cpp, lose_fade.cpp) bound by GameMode definitions.
+- [ ] T031 [US3] Capture session telemetry to `firmware/shared/scripts/log_session_events.py` for post-run analysis.
+
+**Checkpoint**: Real-time gameplay feedback delivered; P1-P3 stories independently testable.
+
+---
+
+## Phase 6: User Story 4 - Betreiber verwaltet System-Updates (Priority: P3)
+
+**Goal**: Enable OTA firmware propagation from master ESP32 to client displays with failure reporting.
+
+**Independent Test**: Upload new firmware to master ESP32, trigger update via options menu/API; verify all client nodes report new version or flagged retry path.
+
+### Implementation for User Story 4
+
+- [ ] T032 [US4] Implement OTA command broadcast in `firmware/esp32/main/ota_manager.c` notifying clients via RS485 and Wi-Fi.
+- [ ] T033 [US4] Add ESP32 client OTA handler `firmware/esp32/components/client_fw/ota_client.c` to fetch `ota/latest.bin` and report status.
+- [ ] T034 [US4] Update Arduino to pause gameplay during OTA cycle in `firmware/arduino/src/ota_guard.cpp`.
