+- **FR-001**: The console MUST allow Player 1 to progress from idle to gameplay solely through touch navigation and player button confirmations.
+- **FR-002**: The system MUST load game definitions from SD-card content and only present games whose `min/max` player counts match the active selection.
+- **FR-003**: LED segment assignments and display seat labels MUST follow the mappings documented in the segment map, including Joker exclusion for five-player sessions when disabled.
+- **FR-004**: Every ready screen MUST require explicit confirmation from each participating player’s hardware button before gameplay can begin.
+- **FR-005**: During gameplay, the system MUST collect scores, update ring animations, and show ranked results plus replays upon completion.
+- **FR-006**: At startup and before starting a session, the system MUST validate the SD manifest hash against all ESP/Arduino nodes and block gameplay if mismatches exist.
+- **FR-007**: The admin options menu MUST expose diagnostics for RS485, Wi-Fi, LED tests, display tests, and error logs, providing actionable feedback within two minutes.
+- **FR-008**: The system MUST log any invalid or missing SD files, hardware faults, or synchronization failures to a retrievable diagnostics history for operators.
 
 ### Key Entities *(include if feature involves data)*
 
-- **[Entity 1]**: [What it represents, key attributes without implementation]
-- **[Entity 2]**: [What it represents, relationships to other entities]
+- **GameDefinition**: Describes a playable mode, including identifiers, player count range, LED usage rules, required hardware capabilities, phase timing, and linked option bundles.
+- **OptionBundle**: Groups user/admin configuration fields (e.g., Joker color, countdown style), defines scope (user/admin/system), and references the subsystems affected by each option.
+- **PlayerSlot**: Represents a seat in the ring, storing display ID assignment, SpielLED start/end groups, boundary LED references, and Joker overrides.
+- **HardwareNode**: Tracks each ESP32 or Arduino participant, capturing role (master/client), firmware version, last heartbeat, and synchronization status.
+- **ManifestEntry**: Records the relative file path, semantic version, SHA-256 hash, and compatibility metadata for every SD asset loaded at runtime.
+
+## Assumptions
+
+- Up to six players participate simultaneously; additional players are out of scope.
+- Game and option JSON files are authored using the provided schemas and validated before deployment.
+- Hardware test bundles derived from official Waveshare demos are available for every subsystem before integration builds.
+- Network connectivity is limited to trusted local Wi-Fi; remote/cloud integrations are future work.
 
