+# Implementation Plan: PitterOmat v2 product requirements
+
+**Branch**: `003-define-product-requirements` | **Date**: 2025-10-20 | **Spec**: [spec.md](./spec.md)  
+**Input**: Feature specification from `/specs/003-define-product-requirements/spec.md`
+
+**Note**: This plan follows the workflow in `.specify/templates/commands/plan.md`.
+
+## Summary
+
+Deliver the venue-ready LichtLoser experience across all 12 ESP32 displays and the Arduino-driven LED ring by formalizing Idle → Menu → Game flows, Quickstart replay, admin-governed ambience controls, and debug tooling. Work builds on existing firmware stacks (ESP-IDF + LVGL and Arduino) with new coordination logic, persistence for session/ticker data, and compliance-verifiable tests aligned to constitution principles.
+
+## Technical Context
+
+**Language/Version**: ESP-IDF C (5.1) for ESP32-S3, C++17 via Arduino core for Mega 2560, Python 3.11 for tooling scripts  
+**Primary Dependencies**: ESP-IDF + FreeRTOS, LVGL 8.3 UI assets, Arduino core, CBOR serialization (tinycbor), manifest_tool Python package  
+**Storage**: SD card (FATFS) for manifests/config, ESP32 NVS flash for session cache  
+**Testing**: On-device smoke suites (ESP-IDF Unity runner), Arduino integration sketches, Python-based manifest validation, manual QA per quickstart  
+**Target Platform**: Waveshare ESP32-S3-Touch-LCD-4 (master + 11 slaves) and Arduino Mega 2560 via MAX485  
+**Project Type**: Embedded multi-controller system (master-slave displays + LED controller)  
+**Performance Goals**: Idle → Menu transition ≤3 s, inter-display drift ≤100 ms, WiFi broadcast latency ≤20 ms, Quickstart relaunch ≤5 s  
+**Constraints**: LED brightness ≤55%, display brightness 10–100%, admin auto-lock 10 ±1 s, Joker active only at 5 players, WiFi for ESP-ESP communication, RS485 for ESP-Mega  
+**Scale/Scope**: 12 coordinated displays, up to 6 concurrent players, single cabinet deployment scaling to multiple venues post validation
+
+## Constitution Check (Gate 1)
+
+- **Principle I**: Manifest_tool validates SD assets; Quickstart/session persistence writes update associated manifest entries before release.  
+- **Principle II**: Options and session entities defined against shared schemas (see `data-model.md`); admin edits respect compatibility (e.g., Joker guard).  
+- **Principle III**: Hardware smoke suites reuse vendor demos from `TREIBER/` and archive logs into `tests/succeeded/` after each subsystem run.  
+- **Principle IV**: Seat mapping pulled from `pitteromat.txt`; LED cap enforcement and Joker behavior traced through FR-004/007 and success criteria.  
+- **Principle V**: Master ESP orchestrates UDP broadcast + TCP acknowledgement; admin PIN workflow locks in 10 s; sync status surfaced in UI.  
