l activation.\n3. **Arduino LED Controller**\n   - Add commands for quintic spin curves, brightness clamping, and Joker highlighting.\n4. **Testing & Validation**\n   - Expand Unity smoke tests for sync drift and admin timeout.\n   - Archive successful hardware bundle logs into `tests/succeeded/`.\n5. **Documentation & Manifest**\n   - Update manifest descriptions for new assets and config files.\n   - Refresh `config/admin/news_ticker.json` sample and thermal safety notes.\n\n*Exit Criteria*: All constitution principles verified through tests or documentation, quickstart checklist executed, and `/speckit.tasks` ready for detailed work breakdown.\n\n### Risks & Mitigations\n- **WiFi congestion**: Provide configurable resend window and instrumentation in debug overlay; fall back to TCP for critical actions.  \n- **LED thermal load**: Clamp brightness in firmware and log attempts to exceed 55% for audit.  \n- **Admin misuse**: Auto-lock timer plus audit trail for changes (store `updatedAt` in config bundle).  \n- **Debug overlay leakage**: Auto-hide on new session start (captured in data model and success criteria).\n\n### Milestones\n1. **M1 - Sync Core Ready**: UDP/TCP channels operational, displays stay within drift budget.  \n2. **M2 - Admin Workflow Complete**: PIN gate, ambience controls, ticker editing, and persistence verified.  \n3. **M3 - Gameplay Validation**: LichtLoser spin, Joker logic, Quickstart replay all pass QA.  \n4. **M4 - Release Candidate**: All tests archived, documentation updated, readiness for `/speckit.tasks` and implementation kickoff.\n'@; Set-Content -Path $path -Value $plan.TrimStart()"]}
