+
+# Tasks: PitterOmat v2 product requirements
+
+**Input**: Design documents from `/specs/003-define-product-requirements/`  
+**Prerequisites**: plan.md (completed), spec.md (completed), research.md, data-model.md, contracts/cabinet-api.yaml, quickstart.md
+
+**Tests**: Include Unity smoke tests and integration scripts only where called out.
+
+**Organization**: Tasks are grouped by user story to enable independent implementation and testing.
+
+## Format: `[ID] [P?] [Story] Description`
+- `[P]`: Parallel-safe (different files, no shared state)
+- `[Story]`: User story label (e.g., US1, US2, US3)
+- Include concrete file paths in descriptions and cite the constitution principle satisfied where relevant.
+
+## Phase 1: Setup (Shared Infrastructure)
+
+**Purpose**: Prepare shared build dependencies and configuration artefacts before feature work begins.
+
+- [ ] T001 Update tinycbor and manifest includes in `firmware/esp32/main/CMakeLists.txt` (Principle I)
+- [ ] T002 Add editable ticker seed file `config/admin/news_ticker.json` with default payload (Principle V)
+- [ ] T003 Create Quickstart cache stub `runtime/session_last.json` and document schema header
+
+## Phase 2: Foundational (Blocking Prerequisites)
+
+**Purpose**: Core infrastructure that MUST be complete before any user story can start.
+
+- [ ] T004 Add shared protocol definitions in `firmware/esp32/main/include/cabinet_protocol.h`
+- [ ] T005 Implement CBOR encode/decode helpers in `firmware/esp32/main/src/sync/cbor_codec.c`
+- [ ] T006 Build UDP broadcast and TCP ack scaffolding in `firmware/esp32/main/src/sync/channel.c`
+- [ ] T007 Extend RS485 command map for spin/brightness in `firmware/arduino/mega_led_controller/src/cabinet_commands.h`
+- [ ] T008 Create baseline Unity smoke test `firmware/esp32/tests/test_sync_baseline.c` validating master/slave handshake
+
+**Checkpoint**: Foundation ready - user story implementation can begin.
+
+## Phase 3: User Story 1 - Launch a game night session (Priority: P1)
+
+**Goal**: Players move from Idle to Menu to LichtLoser with synchronized displays and deterministic loser selection.  
+**Independent Test**: Run Idle -> Menu -> Game flow on bench hardware and verify drift <=100 ms, single loser, Joker highlight in five-player mode.
+
+### Implementation
+- [ ] T009 [US1] Gate Start control visibility in `firmware/esp32/main/src/ui/idle_screen.c`
+- [ ] T010 [P] [US1] Update LVGL layout for Idle/Menu flow in `firmware/esp32/ui/src/idle_menu_flow.c`
+- [ ] T011 [US1] Broadcast seat overlays from `firmware/esp32/main/src/session/session_controller.c`
+- [ ] T012 [US1] Implement `/sessions` POST handler in `firmware/esp32/main/src/api/session_api.c`
+- [ ] T013 [US1] Aggregate cabinet state for `/state` GET in `firmware/esp32/main/src/api/state_api.c`
+- [ ] T014 [US1] Add quintic spin engine to `firmware/arduino/mega_led_controller/src/spin_engine.cpp`
+- [ ] T015 [US1] Render Joker highlight and skip logic in `firmware/esp32/main/src/render/joker_controller.c`
+- [ ] T016 [US1] Update scoreboard view in `firmware/esp32/main/src/ui/game_score_screen.c`
+- [ ] T017 [P] [US1] Add Unity test `firmware/esp32/tests/test_idle_menu_game_flow.c` covering Idle->Menu->Game timing
+
+**Checkpoint**: User Story 1 delivers the MVP gameplay loop and passes independent testing.
+
+## Phase 4: User Story 2 - Repeat play with Quickstart and player options (Priority: P2)
+
+**Goal**: Hosts replay LichtLoser rapidly while adjusting rounds, speeds, and Joker settings without re-entering all options.  
+**Independent Test**: Finish a session, trigger Quickstart, edit options, and confirm relaunch <5 s with updated settings.
+
+### Implementation
+- [ ] T018 [US2] Persist session parameters in `firmware/esp32/main/src/session/quickstart_store.c`
+- [ ] T019 [P] [US2] Add options UI controls in `firmware/esp32/ui/src/options_screen.c`
+- [ ] T020 [US2] Implement `/sessions/{sessionId}` PATCH handler in `firmware/esp32/main/src/api/session_api.c`
+- [ ] T021 [US2] Wire Quickstart menu action in `firmware/esp32/main/src/ui/quickstart_button.c`
+- [ ] T022 [P] [US2] Add Unity test `firmware/esp32/tests/test_quickstart_resume.c` verifying cache restore
+
+**Checkpoint**: User Story 2 enables rapid replay with configurable options and validated cache behaviour.
+
+## Phase 5: User Story 3 - Configure cabinet ambience and protections (Priority: P2)
+
+**Goal**: Administrators adjust lighting, palettes, and safety caps with enforced PIN gating and telemetry of changes.  
+**Independent Test**: Enter admin mode, modify brightness and palettes, observe clamp at 55%, verify auto-lock within 10 ±1 s.
+
+### Implementation
+- [ ] T023 [US3] Implement admin PIN timer and relock in `firmware/esp32/main/src/admin/pin_gate.c`
+- [ ] T024 [P] [US3] Persist ambience settings in `firmware/esp32/main/src/config/config_store.c`
+- [ ] T025 [US3] Add LVGL admin screens in `firmware/esp32/ui/src/admin_settings_screen.c`
+- [ ] T026 [US3] Implement `/admin/settings` PATCH handler in `firmware/esp32/main/src/api/admin_api.c`
+- [ ] T027 [US3] Implement `/admin/ticker` POST handler writing to `config/admin/news_ticker.json`
+- [ ] T028 [US3] Auto-hide debug overlay on session start in `firmware/esp32/main/src/debug/debug_overlay.c`
+- [ ] T029 [P] [US3] Add Unity test `firmware/esp32/tests/test_admin_pin_timeout.c` ensuring 10s relock
+
+**Checkpoint**: User Story 3 locks down admin controls and satisfies safety governance requirements.
+
+## Final Phase: Polish and Cross-Cutting Concerns
+
+- [ ] T030 Document updated workflows in `specs/003-define-product-requirements/quickstart.md`
+- [ ] T031 Update manifest entries for new assets in `sd/manifest.json`
+- [ ] T032 Archive validation logs in `tests/succeeded/README.md` with references to new smoke suites
+- [ ] T033 Run end-to-end operator dry run and capture notes in `docs/release-notes/pitteromat_v2.md`
+
+## Dependencies and Execution Order
+
+- Foundational Phase (T004-T008) depends on Setup (T001-T003) and blocks all user stories.
+- User Story 1 (T009-T017) depends on Foundational completion.
+- User Story 2 (T018-T022) depends on User Story 1’s session infrastructure.
+- User Story 3 (T023-T029) depends on Foundational tasks plus shared state from User Story 1.
+- Polish tasks (T030-T033) depend on completion of targeted user stories.
+
+## Parallel Execution Examples
+
+- After T006 completes, T010 and T011 can progress in parallel (UI vs session broadcast).
+- T014 (spin engine) and T015 (render logic) can proceed concurrently once T007 lands.
+- During User Story 2, T019 (UI) and T020 (API) can run in parallel after T018 seeds storage.
+- In User Story 3, T024 (config persistence) and T025 (UI) can advance simultaneously after T023 finishes.
+
+## Implementation Strategy
+
+### MVP First (User Story 1)
+1. Complete Setup and Foundational phases.
+2. Deliver User Story 1 tasks (T009-T017).
+3. Validate Idle -> Menu -> Game loop with Unity test and bench run.
+
+### Incremental Delivery
+1. Ship MVP (US1) to venue alpha testers.
+2. Layer Quickstart enhancements (US2) and revalidate cache behaviour.
+3. Add admin ambience controls (US3) once base gameplay is stable.
+4. Close with polish tasks and documentation updates.
+
+### Parallel Team Strategy
+- Developer A: Sync infrastructure (T004-T006) then gameplay controllers (T011, T015).
+- Developer B: LVGL UI flows (T010, T019, T025) and admin screens.
+- Developer C: API endpoints (T012, T020, T026) and Unity smoke tests (T017, T022, T029).
+- Developer D: Arduino spin engine (T014) and RS485 protocol (T007), plus manifest/documentation tasks.
