[2m2025-10-21T15:24:21.891560Z[0m [32m INFO[0m ToolCall: shell {"command":["powershell.exe","-NoLogo","-Command","Set-Content -Path 'specs/003-define-product-requirements/tasks.md' -Value @'\n---\ndescription: \"Task list for implementing PitterOmat v2 product requirements\"\n---\n\n# Tasks: PitterOmat v2 product requirements\n\n**Input**: Design documents from `/specs/003-define-product-requirements/`  \n**Prerequisites**: plan.md (completed), spec.md (completed), research.md, data-model.md, contracts/cabinet-api.yaml, quickstart.md\n\n**Tests**: Include Unity smoke tests and integration scripts only where called out.\n\n**Organization**: Tasks are grouped by user story to enable independent implementation and testing.\n\n## Format: `[ID] [P?] [Story] Description`\n- `[P]`: Parallel-safe (different files, no shared state)\n- `[Story]`: User story label (e.g., US1, US2, US3)\n- Include concrete file paths in descriptions and cite the constitution principle satisfied where relevant.\n\n## Phase 1: Setup (Shared Infrastructure)\n\n**Purpose**: Prepare shared build dependencies and configuration artefacts before feature work begins.\n\n- [ ] T001 Update tinycbor and manifest includes in `firmware/esp32/main/CMakeLists.txt` (Principle I)\n- [ ] T002 Add editable ticker seed file `config/admin/news_ticker.json` with default payload (Principle V)\n- [ ] T003 Create Quickstart cache stub `runtime/session_last.json` and document schema header\n\n## Phase 2: Foundational (Blocking Prerequisites)\n\n**Purpose**: Core infrastructure that MUST be complete before any user story can start.\n\n- [ ] T004 Add shared protocol definitions in `firmware/esp32/main/include/cabinet_protocol.h`\n- [ ] T005 Implement CBOR encode/decode helpers in `firmware/esp32/main/src/sync/cbor_codec.c`\n- [ ] T006 Build UDP broadcast and TCP acknowledgement channels in `firmware/esp32/main/src/sync/channel.c`\n- [ ] T007 Extend RS485 command map for spin/brightness in `firmware/arduino/mega_led_controller/src/cabinet_commands.h`\n- [ ] T008 Implement LED brightness clamp guard in `firmware/arduino/mega_led_controller/src/brightness_guard.cpp` (Principle IV)\n- [ ] T009 Integrate clamp enforcement pipeline in `firmware/esp32/main/src/render/brightness_manager.c`\n- [ ] T010 Implement idle energy saver controller in `firmware/esp32/main/src/ui/idle_energy_saver.c`\n- [ ] T011 [P] Add Unity smoke test `firmware/esp32/tests/test_sync_baseline.c` validating master/slave handshake\n- [ ] T012 [P] Add Unity test `firmware/esp32/tests/test_brightness_clamp.c` ensuring 55% cap enforcement\n- [ ] T013 [P] Add Unity test `firmware/esp32/tests/test_idle_energy_saver.c` verifying dimming within 10 s\n\n**Checkpoint**: Foundation ready - user story implementation can begin.\n\n## Phase 3: User Story 1 - Launch a game night session (Priority: P1)\n\n**Goal**: Players move from Idle to Menu to LichtLoser with synchronized displays and deterministic loser selection.  \n**Independent Test**: Run Idle -> Menu -> Game flow on bench hardware and verify drift <=100 ms, single loser, Joker highlight in five-player mode.\n\n### Implementation\n- [ ] T014 [US1] Gate Start control visibility in `firmware/esp32/main/src/ui/idle_screen.c`\n- [ ] T015 [P] [US1] Update LVGL layout for Idle/Menu flow in `firmware/esp32/ui/src/idle_menu_flow.c`\n- [ ] T016 [US1] Broadcast seat overlays from `firmware/esp32/main/src/session/session_controller.c`\n- [ ] T017 [US1] Implement `/sessions` POST handler in `firmware/esp32/main/src/api/session_api.c`\n- [ ] T018 [US1] Aggregate cabinet state for `/state` GET in `firmware/esp32/main/src/api/state_api.c`\n- [ ] T019 [US1] Add quintic spin engine to `firmware/arduino/mega_led_controller/src/spin_engine.cpp`\n- [ ] T020 [US1] Render Joker highlight and skip logic in `firmware/esp32/main/src/render/joker_controller.c`\n- [ ] T021 [US1] Update scoreboard view in `firmware/esp32/main/src/ui/game_score_screen.c`\n- [ ] T022 [P] [US1] Add Unity test `firmware/esp32/tests/test_idle_menu_game_flow.c` covering Idle->Menu->Game timing\n\n**Checkpoint**: User Story 1 delivers the MVP gameplay loop and passes independent testing.\n\n## Phase 4: User Story 2 - Repeat play with Quickstart and player options (Priority: P2)\n\n**Goal**: Hosts replay LichtLoser rapidly while adjusting rounds, speeds, and Joker settings without re-entering all options.  \n**Independent Test**: Finish a session, trigger Quickstart, edit options, and confirm relaunch <5 s with updated settings.\n\n### Implementation\n- [ ] T023 [US2] Persist session parameters in `firmware/esp32/main/src/session/quickstart_store.c`\n- [ ] T024 [P] [US2] Add options UI controls in `firmware/esp32/ui/src/options_screen.c`\n- [ ] T025 [US2] Implement `/sessions/{sessionId}` PATCH handler in `firmware/esp32/main/src/api/session_api.c`\n- [ ] T026 [US2] Wire Quickstart menu action in `firmware/esp32/main/src/ui/quickstart_button.c`\n- [ ] T027 [P] [US2] Add Unity test `firmware/esp32/tests/test_quickstart_resume.c` verifying cache restore\n\n**Checkpoint**: User Story 2 enables rapid replay with configurable options and validated cache behaviour.\n\n## Phase 5: User Story 3 - Configure cabinet ambience and protections (Priority: P2)\n\n**Goal**: Administrators adjust lighting, palettes, and safety caps with enforced PIN gating and telemetry of changes.  \n**Independent Test**: Enter admin mode, modify brightness and palettes, observe clamp at 55%, verify auto-lock within 10 +/- 1 s, and confirm debug diagnostics operate without degrading gameplay.\n\n### Implementation\n- [ ] T028 [US3] Implement admin PIN timer and relock in `firmware/esp32/main/src/admin/pin_gate.c`\n- [ ] T029 [P] [US3] Persist ambience settings in `firmware/esp32/main/src/config/config_store.c`\n- [ ] T030 [US3] Add LVGL admin screens in `firmware/esp32/ui/src/admin_settings_screen.c`\n- [ ] T031 [US3] Implement `/admin/settings` PATCH handler in `firmware/esp32/main/src/api/admin_api.c`\n- [ ] T032 [US3] Implement `/admin/ticker` POST handler writing to `config/admin/news_ticker.json`\n- [ ] T033 [US3] Revert in-flight admin changes on timeout in `firmware/esp32/main/src/admin/pin_gate.c`\n- [ ] T034 [P] [US3] Implement debug overlay toggles and auto-hide in `firmware/esp32/main/src/debug/debug_overlay.c`\n- [ ] T035 [P] [US3] Implement latency probe visualization in `firmware/esp32/main/src/debug/latency_probe.c`\n- [ ] T036 [P] [US3] Implement LED ring diagnostic routine in `firmware/esp32/main/src/debug/led_diagnostic.c`\n- [ ] T037 [US3] Implement SD log export workflow in `firmware/esp32/main/src/debug/log_export.c`\n- [ ] T038 [P] [US3] Add Unity test `firmware/esp32/tests/test_admin_pin_timeout.c` ensuring 10 +/- 1 s relock and rollback\n- [ ] T039 [P] [US3] Add Unity test `firmware/esp32/tests/test_debug_diagnostics.c` covering toggles, latency probe, LED diagnostics, and log export\n\n**Checkpoint**: User Story 3 locks down admin controls, satisfies safety governance requirements, and delivers complete debug tooling.\n\n## Final Phase: Polish and Cross-Cutting Concerns\n\n- [ ] T040 Document updated workflows in `specs/003-define-product-requirements/quickstart.md`\n- [ ] T041 Update manifest entries for new assets in `sd/manifest.json`\n- [ ] T042 Archive validation logs (sync, clamp, energy saver, debug) in `tests/succeeded/README.md`\n- [ ] T043 Capture readability scores and operator approvals in `docs/release-notes/pitteromat_v2.md`\n- [ ] T044 Run end-to-end operator dry run and capture notes in `docs/release-notes/pitteromat_v2.md`\n\n## Dependencies and Execution Order\n\n- Foundational Phase (T004-T013) depends on Setup (T001-T003) and blocks all user stories.\n- User Story 1 (T014-T022) depends on Foundational completion.\n- User Story 2 (T023-T027) depends on Quickstart storage and session APIs delivered in User Story 1.\n- User Story 3 (T028-T039) depends on Foundational tasks plus shared state from User Story 1.\n- Polish tasks (T040-T044) depend on completion of targeted user stories and associated validation.\n\n## Parallel Execution Examples\n\n- After T006 completes, T015 and T016 can progress in parallel (UI vs session broadcast).\n- T019 (spin engine) and T020 (render logic) can proceed concurrently once T007 lands.\n- During User Story 2, T024 (UI) and T025 (API) can run in parallel after T023 seeds storage.\n- In User Story 3, T034-T036 can advance simultaneously after T033 finalises rollback safeguards.\n- Unity smoke tests T011-T013 and T038-T039 can execute in parallel once their corresponding features are implemented.\n\n## Implementation Strategy\n\n### MVP First (User Story 1)\n1. Complete Setup and Foundational phases.\n2. Deliver User Story 1 tasks (T014-T022).\n3. Validate Idle -> Menu -> Game loop with Unity test and bench run.\n\n### Incremental Delivery\n- Ship MVP (US1) to venue alpha testers.\n- Layer Quickstart enhancements (US2) and revalidate cache behaviour.\n- Add admin ambience controls, safety features, and debug tooling (US3) once base gameplay is stable.\n- Close with polish tasks, validation archiving, and operator documentation updates.\n\n### Parallel Team Strategy\n- Developer A: Sync infrastructure (T004-T006), brightness/energy safety (T008-T010), and scoreboard logic (T021).\n- Developer B: LVGL UI flows (T015, T024, T030) and debug overlays (T034).\n- Developer C: API endpoints (T017, T025, T031-T032) and Unity smoke tests (T011-T013, T022, T027, T038-T039).\n- Developer D: Arduino spin/brightness work (T007, T019) and diagnostics utilities (T035-T037), plus documentation tasks (T040-T044).\n'@"]}
